<title>FRANCE: GAN slips after EU conditions.</title>
<headline>GAN slips after EU conditions.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-07-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in insurance group GAN slipped slightly after the European Union gave its green light to a state capital injection under conditions.</p>
<p>The EU said GAN must sell its CIC banking unit, its UIC and UIS property units, halve its foreign commercial interests and sell other holdings for a total value of 2.4 billion francs.</p>
<p>GAN is 80-percent owned by the French state. The new Socialist-led government said earlier this month it would continue the privatisation process of GAN started by the previous government.</p>
<p>At 1012 GMT, GAN shares were down 0.71 percent at 154.10 francs. They wre 0.13 percent down before the European Union announcement, which was as expected.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
